render-ports' table (guest 7892 escape, lab 7893 corp, vm 7894 direct, three
rows the reader drops) against a rendered
host.json that is out of step with it, for `status`'s port lines:

  guest-in 7892   matches the table                 -> a plain line
  lab-in   7895   the table says 7893               -> "NOT in host.json yet"
  (no vm-in)      vm is in the table, not rendered  -> "NOT in host.json yet"
  old-in   7899   no row of that name any more      -> "removed — but host.json still has it"

The host.json is cut down to what those lines read (its inbounds); both
implementations see the same file.
